WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.600
- [Interviewer] All right, Cindy.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.290
- Hi.
- Cindy, where'd grew up?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.750
Where are you from originally?

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.800
- [Cindy] I'm from Oklahoma, 700 Valley.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.310
- [Interviewer] Okay and
tell me about your childhood.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:13.740
You had both of your parents?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.123
- Basically my dad died before I was born,

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.690
right before I was born.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.980
Tragic accident at work or something.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.600
So I never met my dad.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.200
My mom raised me and my two brothers

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.940
and it was basically okay childhood,

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.410
except for the fact that I was touched

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.590
by every one of my uncles.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:34.960
My mom had six brothers

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.010
and basically I know now that she traded

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.790
molestation acts to me for drugs

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.270
and stuff like that
everything came out later on

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.320
and I was even kidnapped

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.980
by one of my uncles for about two weeks.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.590
And I was pregnant with
his child by 10 years old.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:56.410
And I couldn't keep the
baby or nothing like that.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.529
- [Interviewer] You got
pregnant at what age?

00:00:57.529 --> 00:00:58.560
- Ten.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.010
Yeah, I had just started my
period and I didn't even know

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.820
that I was pregnant except that my mom

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.430
kept tabs on like getting me pads

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.600
and stuff like that and
she took me to the doctor

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.433
and I was pregnant.

00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:11.540
I didn't even tell her what happened,

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.970
but I was in a dark
alley, outside my house

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:17.210
and I was kidnapped by
a man in a dark mask

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.610
and raped, brutally raped

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.500
and right before I got out of the van,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.523
I took off the mask and it was my uncle.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:28.730
And basically a couple
other people came forward

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.530
and saw it like neighbors and stuff

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.550
and they told my mom,
they told the detective.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.460
He ended up going to jail
and I had to press charges

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.940
but my mom was really mad at me about it.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.500
So like throughout my whole life,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.870
I didn't really want to tell her anything.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.400
I kept things from her.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.134
'Cause she always made me
feel like it was my fault.

00:01:45.134 --> 00:01:46.210
She always-

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.043
- [Interviewer] So your
mom was an addict but-

00:01:47.043 --> 00:01:47.876
- She was an addict.

00:01:47.876 --> 00:01:48.800
- [Interviewer] But she kept the kids.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.240
- Yeah and she works a
good job and stuff at CSUN

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.700
and so she always kept a good job

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.970
so that's kinda what made me
like always do good in school

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.340
like make it look good on the outside

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.560
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.100
But really my mom, she was a
really bad addict, really bad.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.513
She had alcohol problem too.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.443
I don't know if it was like

00:02:06.443 --> 00:02:08.700
from the loss of my dad, whatever.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.533
Yeah.

00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:12.120
- [Interviewer] And when
do you go out on your own?

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.903
- I've been on my own
probably since I was 23.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.670
I was addicted to sex and stuff and drugs

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.150
and I was just so ashamed
to do that around my family

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:26.220
and of other people to see
me like that, that I knew.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.790
So I came to a different area.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.480
So I came downtown where nobody knew me

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.700
and continued to you
sell my body and stuff

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.570
and I've had opportunities
to like move forward

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:39.400
and do good and stuff, but I chose it

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.060
and I'm not really sure why
but I know that like I'm hungry

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.760
for attention and there's a borderline

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.020
where like it feels good but it's wrong

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.350
and that's attractive to me.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.890
And I think I was just always raised

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.570
feeling like it's wrong what is right.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.600
It's wrong what it feels good

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.500
and it's like, I still live with that.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.160
- [Interviewer] So what
kind of feelings do you get,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.600
shame and guilt and all that?

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.783
- I feel shame and guilt that
I'm not raising my children.

00:03:06.146 --> 00:03:06.979
- [Interviewer] How many kids do you have?

00:03:06.979 --> 00:03:07.823
- Three boys.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.533
- [Interviewer] Who raises?

00:03:09.533 --> 00:03:10.720
- My mom.
- [Interviewer] Your mom.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.180
- And it's sad because I
don't know what's going on,

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.700
with them now, with my mom I mean,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.633
I never trusted my mom ever,
but she makes it look so good.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.460
But I talk to my kids like
every other week and stuff

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.270
over the phone and Skype and stuff so-

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.740
- [Interviewer] Your mom's still using?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.930
- I don't know.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.220
I just, I don't see how she can't.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.300
I know for sure she
uses alcohol every day.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:38.190
That's her thing, but she
uses her having a good job

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.950
and working all day that
she's entitled to drink.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.830
She's entitled to do what she wants,

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.663
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:43.663 --> 00:03:46.020
As long as she's taking care
of everything financially

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.860
and that's kind of like
the role I've taken too.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.080
As long as I take care
of myself financially,

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.330
I can do whatever I want.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.316
- [Interviewer] So today you're
living on the street here?

00:03:55.316 --> 00:03:57.040
- I'm on the street.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.227
- [Interviewer] You're in
a tent here on Skid Row?

00:03:58.227 --> 00:04:02.040
- I'm on a tent and Skid Row
and I have a couple of tents.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.240
I have a boyfriend who's
really controlling,

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.571
kind of like a pimp if you wanna call it.

00:04:07.571 --> 00:04:08.690
- [Interviewer] So that's
how you're making money?

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.110
- Yeah and most of it goes to him

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.860
and he doesn't like what I do,

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.450
but he gets to spend all of it

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:19.510
and it's just like a revolving
circle of going outside,

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:20.900
getting the money, doing the drugs

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:25.400
and going back outside,
all day, every day.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.850
Now even, I mean, I'm missing work,

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.850
but I really wanted to come and do this.

00:04:33.258 --> 00:04:34.091
- [Interviewer] And this has got to get

00:04:34.091 --> 00:04:35.020
depressing for you, right?

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.163
- It's so depressing.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.890
It's very hard.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.480
Every day and to put on a smile
and I mean people know like

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.480
if you're going through something,

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.980
they don't wanna pick you
up, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.730
So I have to look as good as possible

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:52.090
that's why I'm not your
typical looking prostitute,

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.030
you know what I mean?

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:56.540
And I don't dress up all naked or whatever

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.490
and the people who know
me, they're loyal to me,

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.323
you know what I mean?

00:04:59.323 --> 00:05:02.320
And it's more of a conversation
than it is anything,

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.920
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.623
Dare able to see like the
real underneath part of me.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.080
- [Interviewer] You have you
regular customers and stuff?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.420
- I have regular people
that have been coming

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.370
for five years, every week loyally

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.330
and sometimes they don't have
the money, sometimes they do

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.440
and if I see them on the
street and I need something,

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.430
they'll stop and they'll
give me a couple bucks here

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.213
and there or furniture
or anything, blankets.

00:05:26.505 --> 00:05:28.220
I'm willing to do anything just to get by.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.176
- [Interviewer] And
what is your drug today?

00:05:30.176 --> 00:05:31.009
- Its crack.

00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:32.900
- [Interviewer] Crack. How
long have you been using crack?

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.603
- It's going on 23 years.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.640
- [Interviewer] So you started early?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.930
- Yeah.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:38.837
I had an 18 year old boyfriend

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:41.100
and I was like really young at the time

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.750
and he got me started on that

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.883
and I just been in love
with it ever since.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.530
I just, I stopped, I
stopped for a little bit,

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.864
but I always craved to go back.

00:05:51.864 --> 00:05:53.190
- [Interviewer] What did crack do for you

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:54.750
when you first started using it?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:59.750
- It gave me like feeling
sexy and beautiful and mellow,

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.170
horny, all feelings,
sexual feelings to me.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.020
- [Interviewer] And what
does it do for you today?

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.150
- Same thing.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.320
- [Interviewer] Still works?
- Same thing.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.500
- [Interviewer] Okay you're not just-

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.080
- Yeah, but more of, it's
more like a chemical balance

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.223
to me for like a mood stabilizer today.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.930
I don't get as high on it as I used to,

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.370
unless it's really good.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.760
- [Interviewer] It's probably
not as pure as it used to be.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.900
- Right, stomped on, but
it's like, it makes me mad

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.730
'cause I keep going to get it.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.010
Keep going to get it no matter
if it's short, it's bad,

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.613
it's whatever I'm going.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.780
No matter what I'm going.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.970
I don't know for how long.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.670
- [Interviewer] What is, I mean-

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.810
Certainly you're an intelligent woman

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.070
and you see that that's gonna
lead nowhere in your life.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.077
- I know.

00:06:45.077 --> 00:06:46.710
- [Interviewer] But you
can't break free of it.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:47.543
- Yeah.

00:06:47.543 --> 00:06:50.350
- [Interviewer] What do you
think people watching this,

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.430
just don't understand about addiction?

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:57.270
- I think it has a lot to do with me,

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:01.730
my opinion has a lot to do with
family being there for you,

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.100
friends, a good support group,

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.240
because I don't have any of that

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:09.970
and I never have and I guess
that's what I'm missing.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.670
- [Interviewer] Did you
ever feel loved as a child?

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.073
- Not really, no.

00:07:13.073 --> 00:07:13.906
- [Interviewer] No dad?

00:07:13.906 --> 00:07:15.300
- No dad.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.310
I just been on a search for
love and trying to fill a hole

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.683
that can't be filled.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.210
And I don't know what it is.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.210
I don't know if it's God, I
mean, I have God in my life now.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:31.710
I don't feel as empty and I
do have my kids that I talk to

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.000
so I don't feel as empty,

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.250
but I definitely feel
like I'm going nowhere.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.200
I just don't wanna die out here.

00:07:39.844 --> 00:07:40.793
Not like this.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.960
- [Interviewer] Have
you been clean before?

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.120
- I've been clean,

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.370
probably the most for
like three, four years.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:49.090
I've had a steady job,

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:51.690
but then I always end up going back.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.710
- [Interviewer] What sets you
back? What makes you relapse?

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:58.330
- My relapse, I just like the
urge, even going to meetings

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.410
even going to like any meetings

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.210
like I feel like using during any meeting,

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.680
like I don't know, like talking about it,

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:05.180
not talking about it you know.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.410
- [Interviewer] Is it
like a constant battle

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.750
just to not use, even when you're clean?

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:10.990
- Yeah.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.850
'Cause like, I feel good when I'm clean.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:16.340
I like myself better, but I
can't wait to do it again.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:19.170
It's like that constant
like I know it's wrong,

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:20.193
but it feels good.

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:23.333
It's like a never ending story in my life.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.640
Is it wrong because it feels good?

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.293
I grew up with that feeling.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.390
Even in my sex life with my boyfriend

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:34.880
I can't be with him unless we're doing

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.063
some kind of role play based
on my childhood trauma.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.380
I'm constantly asking him
to pretend he's my uncle

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:45.800
or my dad or some kind of family member.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:50.223
It's embarrassing to say, but
that's the truth, literally.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.763
I think he feels bad.

00:08:56.292 --> 00:08:59.240
- [Interviewer] And working
here, picking up guys

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.140
on Skid Row that's dangerous sometimes.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.050
- [Cindy] Yeah.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.350
- [Interviewer] What kind of stuff is?

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.000
- [Cindy] I've been stabbed.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.963
I've been kicked out of cars, beat up,

00:09:09.847 --> 00:09:11.540
drugged, you know what I'm saying?

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:13.590
Just people have stolen my money.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:16.340
Made me do the do and then taking my money

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:20.760
and I've even walked home
with no shoes, no clothes,

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.280
after doing a whole night of job

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:26.023
and it's the worst feeling.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.280
I'm mad at myself, I'm mad at myself.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:32.230
I won't go do this with
somebody I don't know this time,

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:35.400
but when I'm desperate,
it's like I have no choice.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.380
Whatever comes up, you know?

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.850
- [Interviewer] Do you have any friends?

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:40.100
- [Cindy] I really don't.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.740
I think I get to say I have one friend

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:45.840
and I don't know how loyal that person is.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.520
- [Interviewer] What do
you think might help you

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:51.820
get out of this situation?

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.840
- [Cindy] Myself. Just to, I don't know.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.573
I mean God and me, I don't know.

00:09:59.662 --> 00:10:03.210
I'd like to say, oh if I had a
really good job that came up,

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:06.400
or if I moved, but I think
no matter where I would go

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.653
I would search out my drug.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.300
Or I end up working somehow I don't know.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.610
- [Interviewer] Do you think
there's something about this,

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.770
this life that just is
addictive, is attractive?

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.310
- Yeah.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:21.780
Not just the drug its everything.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.210
- [Interviewer] Yeah you
feel like you belong here.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:24.043
- Everything. Yeah.

00:10:24.043 --> 00:10:25.600
- [Interviewer] In this
situation, this life.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.140
- It's so weird 'cause I
know I'm not from here,

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:31.040
but I never felt like I
belonged so much in my life.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:31.873
- [Interviewer] Whereas if you were living

00:10:31.873 --> 00:10:33.180
in a beautiful house somewhere,

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.080
in a nice neighborhood,
beautiful car and family

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:35.913
and everything.
- Exactly.

00:10:35.913 --> 00:10:37.940
I come from money and
now I'm working for it.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.150
- [Interviewer] Do you probably-

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.436
- I didn't need for
anything. I Had my own car.

00:10:41.436 --> 00:10:42.410
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
but if you have that now

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.907
you'd probably sabotage it right?

00:10:43.907 --> 00:10:44.740
- Right.

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:48.210
And it's almost like I'm
like I'm punishing myself

